      "message": {
        "role": "tool",
        "tool_call_id": "call_dqkOsU13nf6nGI2LQD4XdVlg",
        "content": "# stairs\n\nStairs in NetHack come in two glyphs: > for stairs down and < for stairs up. To descend to the next dungeon level, stand ON a > tile and call descend. Critical: < (stairs up) do NOT take you deeper. The goal is to descend through > tiles.\n\nIf descend fails ('you cannot go down here'), you are not on a > tile. Check UNDER PLAYER in the observation — it says 'stairs DOWN' or 'stairs UP' or the tile you are actually on. The @ glyph hides the tile beneath it.\n\nTo find stairs: scan VISIBLE FEATURES (lists every stairs/altar/fountain with (x,y) coords). Call move_to(x, y) to walk to a > tile, then descend.\n\n",
        "name": "ipython"
      },
      "sampled": false,
