        "role": "tool",
        "tool_call_id": "call_S3z1Q3ewChu6nj8hmwBIi08J",
        "content": "# exploration\n\nExploration rewards methodical work. The map starts unrevealed; only tiles in sight are visible. Walking through corridors reveals adjacent tiles. autoexplore walks toward the nearest frontier (a known tile adjacent to an unseen tile).\n\nRecommended workflow on a new dlvl:\n1. autoexplore repeatedly until VISIBLE FEATURES shows stairs DOWN.\n2. move_to(x, y) using the listed > coordinates.\n3. descend.\n\nIf autoexplore reports 'level appears fully explored' but no > is visible, the level has a hidden passage. Walk to a dead-end and call search(times=10). When the harness emits an [autoexplore-loop: N short trips] hint, switch to search or move_to.\n\n",
        "name": "ipython"
      },
